Z||000002||Kwez||09-07-2001||06:03 PM||||I think I wasn't clear in my post,<BR>what I mean is:<BR>is there a break-in period for new shocks like there is for new brake pads / discs etc...<P>ie, for brakes we should avoid hard braking for the 1st few xx miles,<BR>should I avoid hard driving (heavy duty cornering) or roads in very bad condition ?<P>sorry for the vagueness of my 1st post.<P>I just drove the car for the 1st time w. the new shocks & the only diff. so far under normal driving is a smoother ride.<BR>it almost feels like the shocks are softer ! <BR>(I have KYB gas-a-just front & gr-2 rear)<P>oh, and the front is a bit higher than before.<P>before:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.enter-net.com/~pquesnel/88GT/original/Sep03$20.JPG"> <P>after:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.enter-net.com/~pquesnel/88GT/original/Sep07$01.JPG"> <P><BR>thank you<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Kwez (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||1
